<title>SOUTH AFRICA: South Africa union gives notice of trucking strike.</title>
<headline>South Africa union gives notice of trucking strike.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South African Transport and General Workers' Union will serve notice on Monday of a national truckers strike to start on Wednesday, union national organiser Thulani Dlamini said.</p>
<p>This follows a revised wage offer of ten percent (from nine percent) by the Road Freight Employers' Association on Friday which was rejected by union members.</p>
<p>Dlamini said the union would give employers the required 48-hour notice period on Monday and would push ahead with the strike on Wednesday unless there was a better offer.</p>
</text>
